{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Ethan jolted awake to the harsh, synthetic glare of a sun that hung too perfectly in a sky the color of polished steel. Rolling onto his side, he groaned as his fingers sank into the cold, unyielding ground—not grass, not dirt, but something smooth and pixelated, like a giant screen pressed beneath him. His vision flickered for a second, a glitch-like distortion that cleared to reveal a landscape of jagged mountains and endless savannah, dotted with creatures that moved with the stiff, exaggerated gait of NPCs. He flexed his hand and watched in disbelief as his fingers stretched unnaturally, then snapped back into place. Then came the worst part: the health bar above his head, the notification popping into view like a cruel joke. *\"Welcome to procedurally generated survival mode, Player. Objective: Escape or Level Up.\"*\n\nPanicked, Ethan sprinted toward a cluster of stone ruins, only to realize too late that running left a trail of floating, glowing question marks—his lost experience points. Inside the crumbling structure, he found a rusted sword embedded in a torc, its edge flickering with a blue aura. As he gripped it, the world darkened for a split second, and a voice—smooth, mocking—echoed in his skull: *\"You have chosen Strength. Would you like to sacrifice Agility for +10 melee damage?\"* Ethan’s stomach twisted. He knew, with sickening certainty, that there was no \"exit\" button, no way to press \"restore game\" and wake up in his actual bed. The question marks behind him were multiplying. Somewhere, far off, a roaring lion—*boss alert*—paced at the edge of the forest. He had one choice left: play along.", "logprobs": [{"token": "E", "logprob": -1.9033106565475464}, {"token": "than", "logprob": -0.011208427138626575}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.38688793778419495}, {"token": "olt", "logprob": -0.0007765853079035878}, {"token":